## Overview

`taf.ul.marvin` is a Python library for managing Marvin test runs and test cases in automated test environments. 
It provides a high-level interface for preparing, starting, and stopping Marvin, as well as handling test run and test 
case lifecycle operations.

## Marvin UI:
- Production: https://marvin.ou.nsn-rdnet.net/
- Development: https://marvin-dev.ou.nsn-rdnet.net/

## Features

- Download and install Marvin client
- Prepare and start Marvin with custom configuration
- Create, start, and stop test runs and test cases
- Fetch snapshots and manage verdicts
- Integration with utility functions for BTS ID collection and command execution


## Supported Python Versions

This library supports Python versions as specified in the `requires-python` option in [pyproject.toml](pyproject.toml).

## Installation

Follow the generic library installation process described in the [TAF user guide][4].

## Usage

Import the `marvin` interface and use its methods to control Marvin test runs.

Basic usage:<br>
Python:
```python
from taf.ul.marvin import marvin

m = marvin()
m.prepare_and_start_marvin(test_case_name="MyTestCase", marvin_side="dev")
# ... run your test ...
m.stop_marvin(verdict="Passed")
```

Robot:
```Robot Framework 
Library           taf.ul.marvin  WITH NAME  marvin

marvin.Prepare And Start Marvin  test_case_name=MyTestCase  marvin_side=dev
# ... run your test ...
marvin.Stop Marvin  wait_after_run=${False}
```


